  <!-- Conclusion -->
  <section id="conclusion">
    <h2>So What Did I Learn</h2>
    <p>
      Three years of messing with CDNs. Fifteen-ish services tested across different projects. <strong>Cloudflare</strong> is still what I reach for first on most sites. Free tier that's actually useful, solid performance, and the DDoS protection plus free SSL are nice bonuses. Hard to argue with free.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>BunnyCDN</strong> is my go-to when clients watch every penny or when there's video involved. That penny-per-gigabyte thing sounds too good but it's real. Serving 500GB a month for about $5? Yeah that math works out.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Fastly</strong> comes out when enterprise clients need instant cache clearing and have budget for it. Expensive? Sure. But nothing else clears cache globally in 150ms.
    </p>
    <p>
      Look if you don't have a CDN on your site right now just go set up Cloudflare. It takes like 15 minutes and costs nothing. Your visitors from other countries will notice immediately. And this is one of those rare situations where free actually is the right answer for most people.
    </p>

    <div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-ocean-deep/40 to-jet-stream/20 border border-jet-stream/30 rounded-xl p-6 mt-6">
      <p class="text-white font-semibold">My Top Pick: Cloudflare</p>
      <p class="text-white/70 text-sm mt-2">Best overall CDN for most websites. Unlimited free bandwidth, 310+ edge
        locations, built-in security, and it actually works.</p>
      <div class="mt-4">
        <AffiliateButton
            href="/go/cloudflare"
            text="Start with Cloudflare Free"
            subtext="No credit card required"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

